# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/prefix-tiers development window (the preconverted GDN checkpoints and the host KV tier; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/prefix-tiers and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are
# resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-prefix-tiers-1 is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/prefix-tiers head (sed -i 's/tp4-prefix-tiers-1/<tag>/' *.env); every later job serves that one
# image. A commit of a file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# B0 (STOP, no card opened): build the window image from the pushed tp4/prefix-tiers head. Nothing is baked as the image default (no C2_BAKE_DEFAULT_PROFILE): the image is for gate arms and never deployed.
# THE EXTENSION (done, nothing to run): the host tier moves KV blocks with version 2 of the qwen_kv_read extension (ttnn.qwen_read_blocks_raw, qwen_write_blocks_raw, qwen_block_bytes). It was built on the rig by
# build_kv_read.sh into its OWN directory, opgraft-KVR2, beside the untouched version 1 build (opgraft-KVR, which earlier packs pin and mount), and this branch pins it (scripts/ci/pin_kvread.py moved the four
# pin sites: the Dockerfile RUN, build-c2-serving-image.sh, c2_image_provenance.py, test_c2_image_overlay.py). build-c2-serving-image.sh reads opgraft-KVR2 BY DEFAULT on this branch (C2_KVREAD_DIR names another
# directory under the home; unset here), so THIS ENV NAMES NO PATH and the version 1 directory is neither read nor written. The image still calls the directory opgraft-KVR. The build refuses, in this order:
# a directory whose MANIFEST.sha256 does not verify, a .so that is not the pinned hash, the Dockerfile's import check (the module must import with no device and set the four ops), G1 provenance (g).
# A new extension build later needs pin_kvread.py again and a new tag.
# THE IMAGE MUST CARRY THE PREFIX STAGE with the P1b and tier edits: qwen_prefix_stage applies the scheduler, runner and model grafts, and qwen_prefix_model_patch.PATCHED_SHA256 is the model graft's pin (the anchor probe holds the
# served model.py to it before any tier arm boots). Never during a timing job. No privileged builder container may be up.
# READ: the build log's provenance report with no problem line (incl. check (g), the extension at its new pin), the Dockerfile's '[KVREAD] qwen_kv_read 2 ...' line, the closure checks pass, the image id printed. Duration (estimate): 60 minutes. Stop rule.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=build
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-prefix-tiers-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4
